How can I sort a JSON object that contains a list of books in chronological order using the JSON library in Python? The books are stored in a JSON file in the following format:
{
   "books": [
      {
         "title": "To Kill a Mockingbird",
         "author": "Harper Lee",
         "publication_date": "1960-07-11T00:00:00Z"
      },
      {
         "title": "The Catcher in the Rye",
         "author": "J.D. Salinger",
         "publication_date": "1951-07-16T00:00:00Z"
      }
   ]
}
Please provide a Python program that sorts the books by publication date and displays their titles and publication dates. The publication date format is "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ".
[JSON data]:
{
   "books": [
      {
         "title": "The Great Gatsby",
         "author": "F. Scott Fitzgerald",
         "publication_date": "1925-04-10T00:00:00Z"
      },
      {
         "title": "1984",
         "author": "George Orwell",
         "publication_date": "1949-06-08T00:00:00Z"
      },
      {
         "title": "Pride and Prejudice",
         "author": "Jane Austen",
         "publication_date": "1813-01-28T00:00:00Z"
      }
   ]
} 
[JSON code]:
import json
with open('books.json') as f:
    data = json.load(f)
sorted_books = sorted(data['books'], key=lambda k: k['publication_date'])
for book in sorted_books:
    print(f"{book['title']} - {book['publication_date']}")

